{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcing", "label": "Replicated event sourcing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Removes the one-writer-per-persistenceId constraint: multiple replicas of the same entity are active at once on different nodes and each persists independently, with vector clocks detecting concurrent edits and conflict resolvers merging them. It trades simplicity for availability - partial order instead of total, state as fold-plus-resolution, commands validated against the local replica's view. The mental model is CRDT-like for events."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcedactor", "label": "ReplicatedEventSourcedActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## A minimal example", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The base class used instead of PersistentActor. Nothing is passed to the constructor - it reads the Cluster off the ActorSystem."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicaid", "label": "replicaId", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## A minimal example", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "This replica's stable identifier, distinct from persistenceId, defaulting to the node's cluster address. Override only when the id has to survive a re-address (a fixed region name): two replicas that ever share an id dedupe each other's events away, so the default is the safe one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_sharedjournalrequirement", "label": "Shared journal across replicas", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## A minimal example", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The journal must be shared across replicas (Cassandra, shared object storage) for replicated ES to converge."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeswhentouse", "label": "When to use replicated ES", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## When to use it", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The niche pattern: multi-region active-active, edge-style replication, cluster-spanning concurrent writers to the same entity. For typical sharded setups ClusterSharding plus PersistentActor gives exactly-one-writer per key automatically and is simpler."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeswhennottouse", "label": "When NOT to use replicated ES", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": "## When NOT to use it", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sharded entities are simpler when the need is only 'spread entities across nodes'; if 'what wins' has no sensible answer a resolver cannot be written; and replicated ES is eventually consistent, so absolute consistency needs a singleton or sharding instead."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcedactor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcedactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicaid", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_sharedjournalrequirement", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeswhentouse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeventsourcing", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_event_sourcing_overview_replicatedeswhennottouse", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/replicated-event-sourcing/overview.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_replicated_ev